coder › Done. Summary of changes:

- `src/range.ts`
  - Added a `timestamp` helper that calls `Date.parse` and throws `TypeError` (message includes the offending value) when the result is `NaN`.
  - Added a `validate` helper that parses both endpoints and throws `RangeError` when `end < start`.
  - `overlaps` now validates both ranges, returns `false` when either range is zero-length (`start === end`), and uses strict `<` comparisons (`aStart < bEnd && bStart < aEnd`) so the exclusive end is respected and merely-touching ranges no longer overlap.

- `src/range.test.ts`
  - Kept the existing overlapping-ranges test and added tests for:
    - touching ranges → `false`
    - same start instant → `true`
    - zero-length range → `false` against itself and against a containing range
    - unparseable start/end → `TypeError` whose message contains the offending value
    - reversed range (first or second argument) → `RangeError`

